1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,713
In this simulation, a boiler setpoint suddenly reads
ninety-five degrees.

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:07,360
Modbus has no passwords. So who wrote it?

3
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:11,722
This is GhostWire, a safe OT security and troubleshooting
lab.

4
00:00:11,722 --> 00:00:16,510
It uses real Modbus TCP, but only against simulators on
your own computer.

5
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:22,300
It's for technicians and students who have to debug plants
and defend them, without risking real equipment.

6
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:28,352
First, the Silent Sensor. The read times out. GhostWire
never calls that proof.

7
00:00:28,352 --> 00:00:32,250
It lists what was observed, and what is only possible.

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,565
The device documentation says unit seventeen.

9
00:00:35,565 --> 00:00:39,320
Change one setting, retest, and the response is verified.

10
00:00:39,670 --> 00:00:46,070
Every read shows the wire evidence: the exact request and
response bytes, with each Modbus field highlighted.

11
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:51,340
The Giant Pressure teaches that a raw count of thirty-nine
is not thirty-nine bar.

12
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:54,580
With the documented scale, it's zero point three nine.

13
00:00:54,930 --> 00:01:00,555
Now the incident. The traffic log was captured from real
exchanges when the server started.

14
00:01:00,555 --> 00:01:03,090
Eleven reads from the HMI, and one write.

15
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:09,040
The learner types the transaction and the client label.
Wrong guesses earn hints, not answers.

16
00:01:09,390 --> 00:01:15,534
Transaction eleven-eleven, from a maintenance laptop,
changed the setpoint from sixty-five to ninety-five

17
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:19,630
degrees. Then come real-world mitigations, clearly marked
as guidance.

18
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:24,703
A second incident, the Night Scanner: one workstation
sweeps unit IDs one by one.

19
00:01:24,703 --> 00:01:26,860
Find where the reconnaissance starts.

20
00:01:27,210 --> 00:01:28,160
Kiro built this.

21
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:34,695
Two specs with EARS requirements and forty-one tasks, and
correctness properties that became over two thousand

22
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:39,210
property-based test cases per run. One of them caught a
real race condition.

23
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:44,838
Three custom agents: a builder, a read-only security
reviewer, and a scenario author.

24
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:47,880
The reviewer's findings went back to the builder.

25
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:48,803
And hooks.

26
00:01:48,803 --> 00:01:55,110
When we asked Kiro to point the app at a plant address,
the guard hook blocked the edit before it was written.

27
00:01:55,460 --> 00:02:02,020
Tests rerun on every save. Every Kiro session is logged
with its tools, files and credits.

28
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:06,390
GhostWire. Investigate the evidence before you touch a
real system.

29
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:08,130
Open source, and free to try.

